# User-facing documentation

When a commit or feature changes how people **learn or work** with MeteorCloud, update the relevant file under `docs/` in the same change.

## Update docs when

* New or changed **CLI commands**, flags, or workflows (`meteorcli`, `make`, installer)
* New or changed **HTTP/MQTT APIs**, request/response shapes, auth, or contracts
* Enrollment, device lifecycle, MQTT, artifacts, or operator console flows operators must follow
* Deployment, config, or env knobs that change how someone installs or runs the system

## Do not

* Dump implementation details, refactors, or internal renames into docs
* Add long essays, speculative roadmaps, or duplicate OpenAPI verbatim
* Create new doc files unless no existing topic fits; prefer editing the right page under `docs/` (see `docs/README.md`)

## How to write

* Short, actionable: commands, endpoints, config keys, and the minimum context to use them
* Match the tone and structure of nearby docs
* Link related pages instead of repeating them
* If unsure whether something is user-facing, ask before writing a large doc
